Given,
Total wall area (including the lid $\rangle\langle A\rangle=1.0 \mathrm{~cm}^2$
Thickness of wall $(l)=3 \mathrm{~cm}=3 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~m}$
Average temperature outside the box $=30^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$
\begin{aligned}
\Delta \theta & =30-0=30^{\circ} \mathrm{C} \\
L_{\text {fusion (ice) }} & =3 \times 10^5 \mathrm{~J} / \mathrm{kg} \\
K_{\text {thermocol }} & =0.03 \mathrm{~W} / \mathrm{m} \mathrm{K}
\end{aligned}

We know that,

\frac{Q}{t}=\frac{K A}{l} \Delta \theta

For one day, $t=24 \times 60 \times 60 \mathrm{~s}$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{m \times L_{\text {fusion (ice) }}}{t} & =\frac{K A}{l} \Delta Q \\
\frac{m \times 3 \times 10^5}{24 \times 60 \times 60} & =\frac{0.03 \times 1}{3 \times 10^{-2}} \times 30 \\
m & =\frac{0.03 \times 1 \times 30 \times 24 \times 60 \times 60}{3 \times 10^{-2} \times 3 \times 10^5} \\
m & =\frac{77760}{9000}=8.64 \mathrm{~kg}
\end{aligned}

